<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Sept industry orders down 3.6 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Sept industry orders down 3.6 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS Sept 96     Aug 96    Sept 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change	  -3.6	 +0.1	 +1.5</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     -1.3	 +3.9	 -1.6</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		95.7	 99.3	 97.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following month-on-month details:</p>
<p>				    Sept 96     Aug 96   Sept 96 index</p>
<p> Total domestic orders	  -3.2	 -1.4	  87.9</p>
<p> Total foreign orders	   -4.1	 +2.4	 111.4</p>
<p> Intermediate goods	     -2.0	 +1.9	  99.8</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     -2.2	 +0.1	  93.0</p>
<p>	     foreign		-1.7	 +5.5	 115.3</p>
<p> Capital goods		    -4.3	 -3.4	  95.1</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     -5.0	 -4.3	  83.9</p>
<p>	     foreign		-3.6	 -2.4	 113.3</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables     -6.0	 +2.0	  87.1</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     -2.5	 -0.8	  81.7</p>
<p>	     foreign	     -11.5	 +6.7	  98.2</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Aug/Sept 96 with Jun/July 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		     -1.5</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 -4.0</p>
<p> Foreign orders			  +4.0</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +1.5</p>
<p> Capital goods			   -5.5</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    -0.5</p>
<p>Two month comparison Aug/Sept 96 with Aug/Sept 95:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		     -0.5</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 -4.3</p>
<p> Foreign orders			  +6.6</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +2.2</p>
<p> Capital goods			   -4.5</p>
<p> Consumer goods,durables	     +0.3</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
